Global Ceramic, Flooring North America, and Flooring Rest of the World. The company provides ceramic, porcelain, and natural stone tiles products for floor and wall applications; natural stones, porcelain slabs, and quartz countertops, as well as installation materials; floor covering products comprising broadloom carpets, carpet tiles, rugs and mats, carpet pads, laminates, medium-density fiberboards, wood floorings, vinyl tiles, hybrid flooring, and sheet vinyl; and roofing panels, insulation boards, mezzanine flooring products, medium-density fiberboard, decorative panels, and chipboards. It also licenses its intellectual property to flooring manufacturers. The company sells its products under the American Olean, Daltile, Decortiles, Durkan, Eliane, Elizabeth, Feltex, Godfrey Hirst, IVC Home, Karastan, Kerama Marazzi, Marazzi, Moduleo, Mohawk, Pergo, Quick-Step, Unilin, Vitromex, GH Commercial, Hycraft, Lentex Flooring, Leoline, Redbook, EmilGroup, KAI, Ragno, Aladdin Commercial, Durkan, Foss, IVC Resilient Design, Mohawk Group, Mohawk Home, and Portico. It offers its products to home centers, company-owned service centers and stores, floor covering retailers, ceramic tile specialists, e-commerce retailers, residential builders, independent distributors, commercial contractors, and commercial end users. The company was incorporated in 1988 and is headquartered in Calhoun, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mauro  Vandini | President of Global Ceramic Segment | Age 68 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 40K people. Revenue per employee of $266K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $15K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $741 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Mohawk Industries, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $8.8B market cap on $10.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 26%.","The business throws off $616M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.86\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 28\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 1.7%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 19% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (20.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.43181215879578283},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $30.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 39% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 39% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Mohawk Industries' (NYSE:MHK) Strong Earnings Are Of Good Quality","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-durables/nyse-mhk/mohawk-industries/news/mohawk-industries-nysemhk-strong-earnings-are-of-good-qualit","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793959995.553,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.946,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Mohawk Industries (NYSE:MHK) Stock: Insider Suzanne Helen Sells 1,646 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/mohawk-industries-nysemhk-stock-insider-suzanne-helen-sells-1646-shares.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793916638.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.883,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Mohawk Industries (MHK) Holds Margins In Q3, Is The Rally Already Priced In?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-durables/nyse-mhk/mohawk-industries/news/mohawk-industries-mhk-holds-margins-in-q3-is-the-rally-alrea","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793677163.928,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.875,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Insider Selling: Jeffrey S Lorberbaum Unloads $2.94M