e, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 4% falls short of the cost of capital of 9.1%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.55).","It runs a 26% gross margin and converts 6% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 2.86x.","ROE of 4% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.6x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.3% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 1.0x net debt to EBITDA ($856.1M of cash against $2.0B of debt), with interest covered 27.5x.","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.19).","Working capital ties up about 135 days of sales, a drag on cash generation."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -2.8% over 3 years, 2.5% over 5 years and 2.9% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","At current returns, reinvesting 54% of profits supports about 2.2% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -14.4% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 17%.","Capex runs only 0.7x depreciation (4.1% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 8, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own 18.8%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 97%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (52 sales, net $30.7M sold).","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.7% (1.7% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 2.7% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 20.7% of the float, 5.5 days to cover."],"people":["With about 40,500 employees, each generates about $266K of revenue, 0.7x the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 4.8% a year.","That works out to $15K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.3M (9x revenue per employee), 